// ★ C3: A PRECONDITION RELATING TWO PARAMETERS, and the bound travels along it.
//
// Only `j` is bounded by the length. `i` is bounded by `j`, so nothing in this signature says
// directly that `i` is a valid index — the engine has to compose `i <= j` with `j < n` to get
// there. That composition is native to the octagon, which holds `±x ±y <= c`: `i - j <= 0` and
// `j - n <= -1` close to `i - n <= -1`.
//
// It WORKED before this test existed, and that is why the test exists. No corpus program bounded
// a parameter by another PARAMETER — every relational test used a literal or a `.len` — so the
// composition was one refactor away from being lost silently, and the plan still listed C3 as
// unbuilt. A capability nobody exercises is indistinguishable from one nobody has.
func pick(a i32[n], n usize, j usize < n, i usize <= j) i32 {
    return a[i] +% a[j]
}
func main() i32 { return 0 }
